# literal_translation = Zeus, you king, Dodonaean, Pelasgian, you that dwell afar, ruling over wintry Dodona,—and about you dwell the Selli, your interpreters, men with unwashen feet that bed on the ground. In the past truly you heard my word, when I prayed: me you honoured, and did mightily strike the host of the Achaeans; even so now also fulfill you for me this my desire.
