# literal_translation = Myrmidons, you comrades of Achilles, son of Peleus, be men, my friends, and call to mind furious valour, to the end that we may win honour for the son of Peleus, that is far the best of the Argives by the ships, himself and his squires that fight in close combat; and that the son of Atreus, wide-ruling Agamemnon, may know his blindness in that he did not honour at all the best of the Achaeans.
